AUGUST 27, 2026
All I See Is Red
— S, founder of I Like It Deep
My period is bringing out the absolute fucking worst in me right now. I'm livid. I'm beyond fucking pissed off at everything at the moment. I want to scream and cry at the same fucking time. I'm furious at the tiniest little things going on in life. My hormones can suck a fat one. I'm so irritable and upset I don't want to hear anyone talk or be near me.
If I was comfortable in the place I'm renting, I'd just go sit in my room — but there's no AC, so I'm even more irritable with the heat on top of it. I'm one wrong move from snapping like nobody's business at the guy I rent from. I don't know how he sits so comfortably in that house. I can't handle it, and I refuse to. I'm giving my notice next month when I pay him. I'm so done living there.
The pros and cons of not being close to my boyfriend will be the biggest downfall of moving — especially when I don't have a vehicle or a license. It's so fucking stupid how much harder it is to rebuild your life at 38, starting completely from the bottom. I hate struggling. It's so annoying. I expected getting sober would mean things would finally start falling into place, and it's been the complete opposite. Having to prove myself more, acting like being broke is some new trend I'm trying out. Yeah — hitting up the shelves is definitely a new low for me. Is that supposed to humble me? Because it sure as hell didn't work.
I'm attempting to blog right now just to keep myself from snapping off. My jaw is clenched, my body's tight, ready to claw someone's face off at any moment. I'm so uncomfortable with life right now, it's disgusting. This is supposed to be the inspiration for big changes, right? Well how the fuck is anyone supposed to make that happen? I'd love for someone to explain how you make those changes with zero income.
I'm beyond pissed off that this is my life. I should have never admitted to my family that I did drugs — I should've kept that to myself and just stayed where I was, at my job. Doing the right thing completely wrecked my life. I regret it so fucking much, and I hate my life right now. I hate every ounce of it. None of this is where I ever saw myself, and it's miserable being in it. And now I'm supposed to be doing this DBT program for a whole year, which puts me even further behind than I already am. Fuck. It's so annoying.
So then I think — okay, I started this website with the journals, and nothing happens, no sales, nothing. So I start a blog hoping to make money doing that. And now I'm giving affiliate marketing a shot on the site too. What more am I supposed to do with zero income and zero fucks left?
I am so pissed off today, all I see is red. I'm livid that my leftovers got thrown away, and I'm pissed that my only source of food got shut off — my EBT. Yeah. First time in my life I've ever been on state assistance. It's not even embarrassing anymore, because I don't have anything left to be embarrassed about. I want to throw shit like a child at anyone who gets close to me right now. I'm so fucking pissed off.
